Instructions:
- Run "make" or "make all" to compile both minget and minls
- Run "make tidy" to remove the build folder and leave only the runnable files
- Use ./minls or ./minget to run the desired functions
- Run "make clean" to clean all built objects

Notes:
- Used 3 late days on it, worth it
- These programs reliably fail 6 tests, all to do with holes.
    - The one with direct to indirect: I was trying to figure out how 45072 bytes fit into 8 zones. Still not entirely sure.
- There are a few unreliably failed tests, it has to do with 2 bogus characters being printed out before everything else on that test. It may have something to do with the lack of complete free statements. I've added them around wherever I remembered to, but it's highly likely this will affect test performance. Otherwise most will still pass.

